&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Legal Operations designs and operates the systems, workflows, and programs that help Stripe’s Legal organization work effectively at scale. The team partners with Legal practices, Product, Engineering, Sales, and other cross-functional teams to deliver durable operational and technical solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Legal Program Manager supporting Launch Readiness, you will manage contracting-system and workflow changes required for new products, commercial offerings, and other business launches. You will translate launch and Legal-practice needs into clear delivery plans, coordinate work across legal subject-matter experts and technical partners, and guide changes through design, testing, release, and stabilization. Your work will involve contract templates, approval workflows, intake processes, reporting, automation, and integrations across systems like Ironclad, Salesforce, Configure, Price, Quote (CPQ) tools, and other internal contracting tools. You will own the operational delivery of assigned contracting-system initiatives while partnering with technical specialists and engineers on implementation. You will also help establish reusable patterns, documentation, and controls that make future changes safer and more scalable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage contracting-system and workflow initiatives supporting product launches and monetized offerings, translating business and legal requirements into clear scope, milestones, dependencies, acceptance criteria, and delivery plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functional delivery across Product Operations, Legal, Product, Engineering, Sales, Deal Management, and other stakeholders, aligning system changes with broader launch plans and decision dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead changes to contract templates, intake forms, questionnaires, approvals, reporting, automations, and related workflows from design and configuration through testing, deployment, and post-launch stabilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess downstream impacts on contract output, approvals, integrations, data and access controls, reporting, and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain visibility into delivery status, dependencies, decisions, risks, and blockers, escalating launch-critical issues with clear impact assessments, options, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confirm that testing, release documentation, rollback and support plans, and other readiness evidence are complete before production changes are made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop repeatable intake, testing, release, documentation, and change-management practices, including approved patterns and controls that enable safe self-service for appropriate low-risk changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to reduce manual work, improve system reliability, address technical debt, and create reusable solutions across Legal practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Project Management, Legal Studies, Business or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in program management, legal operations, business systems, product operations, implementation, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing cross-functional programs with multiple stakeholders, dependencies, and fixed delivery dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating business needs into structured requirements, workflows, acceptance criteria, and implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with contract lifecycle management, commercial contracting, Customer Relationship Management (CRM) software, workflow, or enterprise business systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating testing, change management, production releases, or implementation readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow revenue, and create new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s ecosystem enables third-party developers and technology partners to extend products such as Payments, Billing, Tax, Checkout, and Workflows. The Ecosystem team builds the Stripe Apps Marketplace and the distribution, platform, and incentive systems that connect businesses with valuable third-party solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to create a compounding ecosystem: better distribution generates merchant demand and stronger partner returns; those returns attract more high-quality apps; and those apps broaden Stripe’s product fit and value to users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an Ecosystem Product Lead to own the strategy, roadmap, and outcomes for Stripe’s third-party app ecosystem, including the Stripe Apps Marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead both sides of the ecosystem: helping businesses discover and adopt trusted solutions, while enabling developers and partners to build successful products on Stripe. You will determine where Stripe should expand ecosystem coverage, improve the merchant journey from discovery through ongoing usage, and establish the product and operating foundations for a high-quality marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision, strategy, roadmap, and success metrics for Stripe’s third-party app ecosystem and Marketplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the highest-value merchant needs and ecosystem gaps by product, segment, industry, and geography; determine when Stripe should build, partner, or enable third parties to address them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the merchant funnel from discovery and evaluation through installation, activation, usage, and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand distribution beyond the Marketplace by surfacing relevant apps across Stripe’s product workflows, onboarding, Dashboard, support, and other high-intent experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve discovery through search, taxonomy, recommendations, personalization, and merchandising.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish marketplace standards for app quality, reliability, security, permissions, support, and data-use transparency so businesses can adopt third-party solutions confidently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create the incentives, analytics, growth tools, and monetization capabilities that help developers build sustainable businesses and continue investing in Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and monitor ecosystem health, including app coverage and quality, merchant conversion and retention, partner success, and incremental value to Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional teams across Engineering, Design, Data Science, Partnerships, Developer Relations, Marketing, Sales, Support, Risk, and Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe’s ecosystem strategy with developers, technology partners, and users, using their feedback and quantitative evidence to guide product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align senior stakeholders around priorities and trade-offs, and communicate progress, risks, and outcomes clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements below. Preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of product-management, engineering, product-focused founder, or equivalent experience, including ownership of a complex product area at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting strategy and driving execution for a platform, marketplace, ecosystem, developer product, or other multi-sided business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success improving acquisition, discovery, conversion, activation, or retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment across user-facing products, technical platforms, partner economics, and marketplace trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading ambiguous initiatives across multiple product, engineering, and business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency with APIs, integrations, developer tooling, and platform products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to define metrics and use qualitative and quantitative evidence to prioritize investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with external developers, technology partners, or enterprise users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including influencing senior stakeholders and leading across organizational boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling an app marketplace, developer ecosystem, or two-sided platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with marketplace search, recommendations, ranking, personalization, or contextual distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing partner monetization, incentives, or revenue-sharing models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise SaaS workflows such as CRM, ERP, ecommerce, support, reporting, or quote-to-cash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, or another regulated technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking a platform or marketplace from 0→1 and scaling its adoption and operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Samsara (NYSE: IOT) is the pioneer of the Connected Operations™ Cloud, which is a platform that enables organizations that depend on physical operations to harness Internet of Things (IoT) data to develop actionable insights and improve their operations. At Samsara, we are helping improve the safety, efficiency and sustainability of the physical operations that power our global economy. Representing more than 40% of global GDP, these industries are the infrastructure of our planet, including agriculture, construction, field services, transportation, and manufacturing — and we are excited to help digitally transform their operations at scale.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 300; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Working at Samsara means you’ll help define the future of physical operations and be on a team that’s shaping an exciting array of product solutions, including Video-Based Safety, Vehicle Telematics, Apps and Driver Workflows, and Equipment Monitoring. As part of a recently public company, you’ll have the autonomy and support to make an impact as we build for the long term.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a defining opportunity for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to build the platform that brings every new Samsara product to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build the monetization primitives every product team depends on, and you will shape what Samsara charges for and how it bundles. Samsara offers a diverse array of products and as we expand to new categories and markets, we’ll need a monetization platform that supports how we scale to meet these needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across the full product suite, from fleet and equipment to the AI products built on top of them.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To understand the range of products this platform supports, review Samsara Intelligence&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/products/platform/ai-samsara-intelligence&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;, our product portfolio &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/products&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;, and our current plans and packaging &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/resources/plans&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a remote position open to candidates residing in the US.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should apply if:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to impact the industries that run our world:&lt;/strong&gt; Your efforts will result in real-world impact, helping to keep the lights on, get food into grocery stores, reduce emissions, and most importantly, ensure workers return home safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You are the architect of your own career:&lt;/strong&gt; If you put in the work, this role won&#39;t be your last at Samsara. We set up our employees for success and have built a culture that encourages rapid career development, countless opportunities to experiment and master your craft in a hyper growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;re energized by our opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt; The vision we have to digitize large sectors of the global economy requires your full focus and best efforts to bring forth creative, ambitious ideas for our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You want to be with the best:&lt;/strong&gt; At Samsara, we win together, celebrate together and support each other. You will be surrounded by a high-calibre team that will encourage you to do your best.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the monetization platform&lt;/strong&gt; that carries a product from beta to general availability: packaging, entitlements, metering, rating, and provisioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own time to market and margin.&lt;/strong&gt; Set the targets, instrument both, and improve them launch over launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define how Samsara prices new AI products,&lt;/strong&gt; including agent work, MCP and API access, and products billed on the results they produce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make unit economics visible at the point of decision&lt;/strong&gt;, so a team can see what a product costs to serve before they set its price.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build each primitive once&lt;/strong&gt;, so product teams ship commercial changes without reinventing metering or entitlement logic.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with Finance, Sales Operations, and Revenue Systems&lt;/strong&gt; to keep what you build billable, reportable, and auditable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion, role model, and embed Samsara&#39;s cultural principles as we scale globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements for the role:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of product management experience shipping products used by external customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A record of owning a business or product metric and changing its trajectory&lt;/strong&gt;, with a before and after you can walk us through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience building platform or infrastructure products that other product and engineering teams depend on&lt;/strong&gt;, including at least one you took from zero to one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical depth sufficient for engineers to treat you as a peer:&lt;/strong&gt; a degree in Computer Science or Engineering, prior experience as an engineer, or demonstrated fluency in system architecture trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with unit economics. You can reason about cost to serve, gross margin, and how a pricing model moves both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive-level communication and presence, comfortable presenting and defending strategy to the CEO, CFO, and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in a North American time zone. Must be able to work NA Eastern Time to work with engineers based in Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We do not require prior experience with pricing, billing, or revenue systems. We hire for technical depth, evidence of building platforms other teams choose to adopt, and a record of owning a number and moving it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An ideal candidate also has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work on entitlement, metering, or billing infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching AI products where inference cost materially affects gross margin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of convincing other product teams to adopt a platform instead of building their own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;The range of annual base salary for full-time employees for this position is below. Please note that base pay offered may vary depending on factors including your city of residence, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. This role is also eligible for an initial RSU grant with no vesting cliff, and ongoing refresh opportunities tied to performance, subject to plan terms and conditions. Learn more about our total rewards and benefits below.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Annual Base Salary&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$130,602&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$219,500 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Total Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Samsara, we build for the people who keep the global economy moving. We want owners, not passengers, which is why &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/company/careers/benefits&quot;&gt;our rewards&lt;/a&gt; are designed to fuel high-impact builders. Our compensation program delivers above-market total compensation through a combination of base salary, performance-based bonus/variable pay, and equity (for eligible roles) in a high-growth public company. We meaningfully differentiate pay for our top performers, who have the opportunity to earn above-market compensation that can outpace the broader market over time.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond compensation, we provide the foundations that enable long-term success: a flexible, employee-led remote model, a professional development stipend, comprehensive health and parental leave plans, and more. If you’re ready to build for the long term and own the outcome, your journey starts here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Flexible Working&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At Samsara, we embrace a flexible working model that caters to the diverse needs of our teams. Our offices are open for those who prefer to work in-person and we also support remote work where it aligns with our operational requirements. For certain positions, being close to one of our offices or within a specific geographic area is important to facilitate collaboration, access to resources, or alignment with our service regions. In these cases, the job description will clearly indicate any working location requirements. Our goal is to ensure that all members of our team can contribute effectively, whether they are working on-site, in a hybrid model, or fully remotely. All offers of employment are contingent upon an individual’s ability to secure and maintain the legal right to work at the company and in the specified work location, if applicable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Belonging at Samsara&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Samsara, we welcome everyone regardless of their background. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, disability, age, and other characteristics protected by law. We depend on the unique approaches of our team members to help us solve complex problems and want to ensure that Samsara is a place where people from all backgrounds can make an impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accommodations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Samsara is an inclusive work environment, and we are committed to ensuring equal opportunity in employment for qualified persons with disabilities. Please email &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:accessibleinterviewing@samsara.com&quot;&gt;accessibleinterviewing@samsara.com&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=&quot;https://forms.gle/DrM6DFQUiSgfPtCVA&quot;&gt;click here&lt;/a&gt; if you require any reasonable accommodations throughout the recruiting process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Commitment to Authenticity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We use &lt;a href=&quot;https://hiretofu.com/privacyPolicy&quot;&gt;Tofu&lt;/a&gt;, a fraud detection tool, to validate the authenticity of applications and protect against identity fraud. This ensures we are connecting with real people and allows us to prioritize genuine candidates. Please see Samsara’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.samsara.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; for more information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fraudulent Employment Offers&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Samsara is aware of scams involving fake job interviews and offers. Please know we do not charge fees to applicants at any stage of the hiring process. Official communication about your application will only come from emails ending in @samsara.com, @us-greenhouse-mail.io or @mail3.guide.co. For more information regarding fraudulent employment offers, please visit our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://samsara.com/blog/avoiding-fake-job-offers&quot;&gt;blog post here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Us&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we are on a mission to help build a better Internet. Today the company runs one of the world’s largest networks that powers millions of websites and other Internet properties for customers ranging from individual bloggers to SMBs to Fortune 500 companies. Cloudflare protects and accelerates any Internet application online without adding hardware, installing software, or changing a line of code. Internet properties powered by Cloudflare all have web traffic routed through its intelligent global network, which gets smarter with every request. As a result, they see significant improvement in performance and a decrease in spam and other attacks. Cloudflare was named to Entrepreneur Magazine’s Top Company Cultures list and ranked among the World’s Most Innovative Companies by Fast Company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Cloudflare, we’re not looking for people who wait for a polished roadmap; we’re looking for the builders who see the cracks in the Internet that everyone else has simply learned to live with. We value candidates who have the instinct to spot a &quot;normalized&quot; problem and the AI-native curiosity to create a solution using the latest tools. Our culture is built on iteration, leveraging AI to ship faster today to make it better tomorrow, while ensuring that every improvement, no matter how small, is shared across the team to lift everyone up. If you’re the type of person who values curiosity over bureaucracy, and that AI is a partner in solving tough problems to keep the Internet moving forward, you’ll fit right in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Available Locations:&lt;strong&gt; London &lt;/strong&gt;or&lt;strong&gt; Austin&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Cloudflare, our mission is to build a better Internet by giving customers control on they might introduce configuration changes so that they are safe, reliable, and predictable at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Product Manager to lead &lt;strong&gt;Safe Change&lt;/strong&gt; for Cloudflare’s control plane. In this role, you will define how customers preview, stage, roll out, monitor, and recover from configuration changes. You will also shape platform foundations that enable internal teams to deploy changes with higher confidence, stronger guardrails, and lower operational risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cloudflare’s control plane converts dashboard and API changes into global network configurations. Today’s enterprise customers expect robust change-management features: deployment previews, gradual rollouts, quick rollbacks, versioning, traffic segmentation, data residency, auditability, and verification of applied state.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own a high-leverage product domain spanning distributed systems, reliability, developer experience, and enterprise governance. Working closely with engineering and product leaders across the entire platform. You will help turn proven deployment safety patterns into reusable platform primitives across Cloudflare.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This technical, highly collaborative role requires navigating architectural tradeoffs with engineers, evaluating risk and compliance with enterprise customers, and partnering with product and go-to-market teams to drive platform adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of a growing team of infrastructure product managers your responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the customer, be it internal or external. Be the champion and voice of customers. Build intimate, personal customer relationships. Bring the customer&#39;s voice into the creation process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the product vision for your area. Ensure that your vision can work not just for your current set of customers, but for 10 or even 100 times your current set.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evangelize the vision so that all stakeholders are aligned, have context and understand where we are going.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make data-driven roadmap decisions.&amp;nbsp; Make tough tactical prioritization decisions based off of data you collect, curate, and disseminate.&amp;nbsp; Build trust with stakeholders by ensuring that your roadmap is understandable and sensible based on the data you present.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure success. Own the measures used to define success for your product. Success measures must be defined at the inception of a product and tracked throughout its lifecycle. Make measures visible to all stakeholders and interpret them into actionable conclusions and new hypotheses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author use cases and prioritize requirements. Translate observations and customer feedback into a prioritized product backlog.&amp;nbsp; Author use cases based on specific real-world product applications and extrapolate detailed product requirements for the scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate across teams. We win or lose as a team. Product managers play a critical role in creating alignment between engineering teams and stakeholders. A collaborative attitude is essential to the job.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Examples of desirable skills, knowledge, and experience&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is customer-focused, data-driven, methodical and thrives in a goal-oriented and data-driven environment.&amp;nbsp; You have a deep technical understanding of the observability space and outstanding communication and collaboration skills.&amp;nbsp; You are able to work with a diverse group, get consensus, and drive the product forward.&amp;nbsp; You are execution focused, you emphasize getting things done while paying attention to important details. You have a passion for building frameworks that scale massively and make it easy for all teams to get the most out of data as you.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of previous product management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain expertise in making deployment decisions based on data.&amp;nbsp; You have been there, done that as either an architect or product owner for safe change or very closely related technology space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distributed systems experience that allows you to drive the scaling strategy for deployment as our scale grows both on volume and number of internal customers supporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting new products and features to customers – whether as a developer, analyst or product manager. You are enthusiastic about taking something you have helped build and sharing it with the world&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer and stakeholder empathy. You must be the voice of engineering, customers, support, or ops at any given time. You must be able to channel many points of view into a strategic roadmap and deliverables that provide elegant solutions to all requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication, presentation, organizational and analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead, drive consensus and deliver in a matrixed organization with multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large and complex data sets (SQL, Postgres, Prometheus, etc.).&amp;nbsp; You are skilled at proving points with data and can quickly show others how to do so.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with telemetry pipelines (Metrics/Traces) and a very good understanding of modern observability platforms&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate complex technical concepts to all audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus points&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS/MS in a technology- or business-related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with deployment platforms, release engineering, progressive delivery, feature flags, GitOps, IaC, or incident management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in networking, security, CDN, edge computing, observability, or large-scale SaaS environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with APIs, CLIs, telemetry tools, or scripting (e.g., Python, Go, JavaScript).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building platform capabilities adopted by multiple product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with enterprise customers subject to strict change-management, compliance, or data residency mandates.&lt;/li&gt;
